//? Title: Crank–Nicolson: Heat Diffusion, Actual Solves and Oscillating Stable Modes
//? Subtitle: A one-point control, the original sixty-interior-point sine experiment, and separate space/time refinement
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Crank–Nicolson averages the spatial heat operator at consecutive time levels.
For constant nonnegative diffusivity and homogeneous Dirichlet boundaries,
its central-difference sine modes have amplification magnitude at most one
for every positive time step. This norm stability permits large steps, yet
large steps can reverse signs and damp stiff modes poorly. We begin with a
single interior point whose first two values are −0.6 and 0.36, expose the
actual native right-hand sides and reusable Thomas factors, then retain the
original sixty-point sine experiment. Independent modal references separate
spatial discretization error, time integration error and solve rounding.
Separate refinement studies demonstrate second-order behavior without confusing
a small residual or one fortunate error cancellation with PDE accuracy.
)

\toc

> A heat problem small enough to solve by hand

Consider u_t=D u_xx on 0<x<L, with u(0,t)=u(L,t)=0. Use nx interior
points, h=L/(nx+1), and time step τ. Put r=Dτ/(2h²). Averaging the old
and new central differences gives

\[
-r u_{i-1}^{n+1}+(1+2r)u_i^{n+1}-r u_{i+1}^{n+1}
=r u_{i-1}^{n}+(1-2r)u_i^{n}+r u_{i+1}^{n}.
\]
\alttext(The new-time tridiagonal stencil has coefficients minus r, one plus twice r, minus r. The old-time right side has r, one minus twice r, r.)

With one interior point, L=D=1 and τ=1, h=1/2 and r=2. Both neighbors
are fixed zero, so 5u^(n+1)=−3u^n. Starting from u^0=1 gives u^1=−0.6
and u^2=0.36. The magnitude decays while the sign alternates. The physical
nonnegative heat solution cannot do this, so numerical stability alone has
already failed to guarantee positivity or an accurate transient.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/crank_nicolson_one_point.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::crank_nicolson_heat_trace([](double){return 1.;},1,1,1,1,4);
  if(std::abs(t.states[1].profile[1]+.6)>1e-15 || std::abs(t.states[2].profile[1]-.36)>1e-15 || t.factorizations!=1 || t.solves!=4) return 1;
  std::print("| level | actual interior value | actual RHS before elimination | interior RMS | scaled solve residual |\n| ---: | ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& s:t.states) std::print("| {} | {:.6f} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.2e} |\n",s.index,s.profile[1],s.rhs,s.rms,s.scaled_residual);
  std::print("\nActual pivot {}; factorizations {}; complete solves {}.\n",t.pivots,t.factorizations,t.solves);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1050);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2;box.height=1.05;box.font_size=19;
  d.text({3,2.1},"One unknown, two exact zero boundaries: r=2",23);
  for(std::size_t level=0;level<3;++level) {
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<3;++i) {
      box.fill=i==1?dm::graphics::RGB{219,234,254}:dm::graphics::RGB{243,244,246};
      d.node(std::format("u{}_{}",level,i),{3.*i,-2.*level},std::format("x={:.1f}\nu={:.2f}",t.coordinates[i],t.states[level].profile[i]),box);
    }
    if(level) d.edge(std::format("u{}_1",level-1),std::format("u{}_1",level));
  }
  d.text({3,-5.5},"Actual update: RHS = -3 u_old; divide by pivot 5",20)
   .save_svg("build/crank_nicolson_one_point.svg");
  const auto killed=dm::algorithms::crank_nicolson_heat_trace([](double){return 1.;},1,1,1,.25,1);
  if(killed.states[1].profile[1]!=0) return 1;
  std::print("At tau=0.25, r=0.5 and the same one-point mode becomes exactly zero in one step.\n");
}
```
